<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Sufi dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1361 CE – 1388 CE (approx.) · capital Urgench</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Qungrat dynasty that ruled Khwarazm from Urgench in the late 14th century until Timur destroyed the city.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> fell into civil war after 1359, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-sufi">Husayn Sufi</a>, a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qungrat">Qungrat</a> tribe, made himself independent ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> around 1361, with his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurganj">Urgench</a> (Gurganj). He also seized southern Khwarazm, including Kath and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> claimed for the Chagatai lands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Sufids ruled a rich trading oasis on the routes between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurganj">Urgench</a> was a large city of mosques and mausoleums. They allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, who campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> several times from 1372, besieging Urgench in 1373 and marrying his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir-mirza">Jahangir</a> to a Sufid princess, Khanzada.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After repeated revolts, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurganj">Urgench</a> in 1388, levelled the city and ordered barley sown on its site. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>, and Urgench was later partly rebuilt.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sufi-dynasty.jpg" alt="Sufi dynasty" width="320" height="322"><figcaption>Image: 1405-1409 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Contemporary_portrait_of_Khanzade,_in_Timurid_genealogy_1405-1409_(Topkapi_Sarayi_M%C3%BCzesi,_H2152)_f.32a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1361 CE – 1388 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Urgench</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Husayn Sufi, Yusuf Sufi, Sulayman Sufi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chagatai Turkic, Khwarazmian Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sufids, Sufid dynasty of Khwarazm</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1374&amp;focus=sufi-dynasty" aria-label="Sufi dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6158 697 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sufi dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6478 953L6352 637M6478 953L6582 1190"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6352 637h0M6582 1190h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6478 953h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6478 953h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Urgench. <a href="/atlas?year=1374&amp;focus=sufi-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
